# =============================================================================
# i3c_target.pdc  -  Physical constraints for the I3C Target on Certus-NX
#
# NO PIN LOCATIONS: this is an IP-core build, Radiant does not insist on them
# and PAR auto-places every pad (result: reports/i3c_target_impl_1.pad). Add
# ldc_set_location lines here for a real board.
#
# The one thing set here is electrical and independent of the pinout: the Nexus
# default for an unconstrained pad is PULLMODE=DOWN, which is wrong on an I3C
# bus (SDA/SCL idle High through the Controller's pull-up / high-keeper; a
# Target-side pull-down fights it). Turn the weak pull off on both bus pads.
# OPENDRAIN stays OFF on SDA: I3C needs push-pull drive in SDR data phases; the
# core produces open-drain behaviour by only ever driving Low in those phases.
# =============================================================================
ldc_set_port -iobuf {PULLMODE=NONE} [get_ports SDA]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {PULLMODE=NONE} [get_ports SCL]
